  "multiInstance": {
    "_why": "Two instances of the SAME block on one page catch per-render collisions (shared ids, redeclared top-level functions) that a single instance can never surface. The builder gives each sgs/nav-drawer a distinct drawerRef (its dialog id), because the block defaults to 'sgs-nav-drawer' and two dialogs must not share an id. sgs/nav-bar-menu's own drawerRef is an sgs_drawer post id, so a burger on this page always targets the default id: the page checks per-render collisions, not burger-to-second-drawer binding.",
